			"Message": "chore(Element): Advance Cocoon with Language and Window API handlers\n\nUpdate the Element submodule to commit b1de8927, incorporating critical bridges between the Cocoon extension host and the Mountain native backend.\n\nThis update introduces the `RegisterProvider` mechanism to create auto-assigned handles, notify Mountain via gRPC (`Context.SendToMountain`), and return disposables for VS Code-compliant Language Providers. It adds `UriKey` for URI normalization to prevent diagnostic collisions and `MakeEventSubscriber` to standardize `this` binding for Window events. Furthermore, central Map registries are established for Tree Data, Webview View, and Custom Editor providers to ensure efficient O(1) lookups and state synchronization.\n\nThese changes enable the extension host to fully manage providers and events, completing the IPC bridge required for VS Code extension compatibility within the Land architecture.",
